# AGENTS.md — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Read this first. This file is the binding work contract for agents operating in this repository. `CLAUDE.md` is a thin redirect to this file; keep durable guidance here and in the nearest child `AGENTS.md`.

## Repository Contract

- Tracked source, maintained documentation, and reviewed configuration are durable repository truth.
- Generated reports, run state, logs, caches, build products, and scratch work belong under the ignored `/.styrir/` workspace.
- Git source history and Beads/Dolt tracker history are separate. Do not report either as synchronized unless its own remote operation succeeds.
- **Verified completion has standing publication authority:** create a focused local Git commit, close only Beads whose acceptance criteria are satisfied, push Beads/Dolt to its configured `origin`, push Git non-force to its configured `origin`, verify both refs, and leave the checkout clean without asking for redundant approval. Keep incomplete tasks and unfinished parent epics open. A current operator instruction may pause publication for a tranche. Remote creation/replacement, force pushes, destructive history rewrites, deployment, and other newly shared or destructive actions remain separately approval-gated.
- Do not fabricate live state, tests, receipts, integrations, metrics, or verification.

## Work Guidance

- Read the applicable root and child `AGENTS.md` chain before editing.
- Use Beads for work that must survive the current session; read `agent-guidance/beads-and-dolt.md` first.
- When work hits a new issue (a new failure mode, unfamiliar API behavior, or surprising live evidence), research it before briefing a fix: dispatch scouts using the `styrir-search-plus` skill and, when the issue is code-related, also fetch current library/API documentation with Context7. Fold the findings into the fix brief. Known, already-researched issues do not need a new pass.
- When research or new evidence changes the approach, update the plan and the tracker in the same step, before any implementation brief is dispatched: amend the affected Beads (description, acceptance criteria, notes) or create new Beads and supersede the old ones with a reason, so the plan, Beads and briefs all describe the same approach. Never leave a Bead describing an abandoned approach; see `agent-guidance/beads-and-dolt.md`.
- Read `agent-guidance/handoffs.md` when work crosses sessions, agents, or operators.
- Read `agent-guidance/styrir-workspace.md` before creating generated artifacts.
- Read `agent-guidance/gitnexus.md` before architecture exploration, flow tracing, or blast-radius analysis.
- Read `agent-guidance/non-interactive-shell.md` before shell operations that can prompt, overwrite, delete, install, or connect externally.
- Create a child `AGENTS.md` when a directory becomes a durable ownership boundary with distinct contracts or verification rules.

## Verification

- Before reporting completed tracked work, perform the standing publication closeout: focused local Git commit, completion notes, close satisfied Beads, `bd dolt push --remote origin`, non-force `git push origin HEAD`, then verify both refs and a clean checkout. Do not close unfinished parent epics or report completion while either history remains local-only.
- Run checks proportionate to the files and behavior changed.
- Confirm generated/runtime files remain ignored.
- Confirm Git and Dolt publication independently before reporting synchronization.
- Report limitations and unverified external state explicitly.

